A||||3||Fiero Hoosier||Rear clip???||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero Hoosier||09-28-2001||10:28 PM||||What is the rear clip? Is it the "bumper" or is it the rear fenders and roof? The reason I ask because I am planning on replacing the rear fender/roof portion on my 84SE tomorrow and am wondering how big a job it is. Do I need to remove the sail panels (that is what you call the quarter windows, right) or will they come off with the fenders/roof.<P>------------------<BR>84 2M4||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||09-29-2001||12:13 AM||||The rear clip is the rear-most upper roof portion, sail panel side parts and upper fender part.  The rear fascia is not part of it.  You can see all which is one piece because the rear clip is all made of hard fiberglass, where as the rear fascia and the lower 1/4 panels are enduraflex.  You will have to remove the sail panels, and the roof.  the roof will be the hardest to do, do a search on "sunroof swap" and you'll read about a few different methods of getting the roof off, if you havent taken one off before.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero Hoosier||09-29-2001||01:02 AM||||Thanks Joe, I had read so many different discriptions that I got a lil' cornfused.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-29-2001||07:49 AM||||There is no real need to remove the roof entirely. All that you need is an inch clearance or so. Just loosen it at the front and rear till the clearance appears. If you don't know how to remove the sails, ASK! (or do a search!)||||reg||1
